<title>USA: Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady-up $1 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls feeder cattle steady-up $1 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers sold steady to $1.00 per cwt higher, compared to last Monday, USDA said . Demand good. Good attendance farmer-feeder-buyers. 85 percent over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 500-600 lbs 83.50-88.50; 600-700 lbs 79.25 -86.75; 700-750 lbs 75.75-82.00; 750-800 lbs 70.00-77.25; 800-900 lbs 70.30-75.60; 900-1000 lbs 65.00-71.00, some fleshy muddy included;   Large 2 Holsteins -</p>
<p>Part load 437 lbs 70.25; 500-550 lbs 65.75 -66.50; 600-700 lbs 60.75-64.00; 800-900 lbs 61.00-62.50; 1000 -1050 lbs 55.75-58.85.</p>
<p>Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 500-600 lbs 74.00-79.50; 600-700 lbs 70.00 -76.25; 700-800 lbs 68.00-75.75, some replacements 776 lbs 77.50; 800 -900 lbs 64.50-70.50. Receipts - This Week 3,650  Last Week 1,173  Last Year 975</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
